---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About emallsoon — Free Seller Calculators & Methodology';
const description =
  'Why emallsoon exists: free, private, no-signup profit calculators for online sellers. How the math works, how fees are sourced, and what is on the roadmap.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/about/">
  <section class="section--tight section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>About</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Calculators built by sellers, for sellers</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          emallsoon exists because every seller makes the same expensive
          discovery: the price on the tag is not the money in your pocket.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>
          Platform fee structures are designed to be felt, not calculated.
          Referral percentages that scale with your price, fulfillment tiers
          that change with a packaging tweak, Offsite Ads that quietly take
          15% of a random quarter of your orders — each deduction looks small,
          and together they decide whether a business works.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most fee calculators online are lead magnets: enter your email, get
          a number, receive drip marketing forever. These tools are the
          opposite. No account, no email wall, no tracking of your numbers —
          every calculator runs entirely in your browser and the math is
          documented right below each one.
        </p>

        <h2>Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          Every calculator starts from the platform's <strong>published fee
          schedule</strong> (Amazon Seller Central, Shopify pricing docs, Etsy
          fee help center) and then does one honest thing: leaves every field
          editable. Fee rates change constantly and vary by category, size,
          country, and plan — a calculator that hides its assumptions is a
          calculator you should not trust. Each tool page shows its formulas
          in plain text, and the <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a> covers the common
          edge cases.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a platform revises its fees, the defaults here are updated —
          but you should always sanity-check against your own account before
          committing real money to inventory or ad budgets.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          There is no account system and no server-side calculation. The
          numbers you type never leave your device. The site is served as
          static files from a CDN; that is the entire infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>Roadmap</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Break-even units calculator — how many sales until fixed costs are covered</li>
          <li>Discount pricing calculator — what a 20% coupon really costs you</li>
          <li>Amazon storage fee estimator (monthly + long-term)</li>
          <li>Platform comparison — the same product on Amazon vs. Shopify vs. Etsy</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Found a wrong default, a broken formula, or a calculator you wish
          existed? The best way to reach us is wherever you found this site —
          and if you found it in a seller community, that community is
          probably where the feedback thread lives too.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
</style>
